  - {id: V28, name: gate ladder green}
  - id: Y01
    name: three node types
    assert: every policy-graph node is typed premise, meta_cu or actor_cu; only
      actor_cu nodes receive determinations; meta_cu nodes gate and are never
      reported as standalone findings; premises never create an obligation
  - id: Y02
    name: per-field spans
    assert: every actor_cu carries a char_span for each populated field and every
      span re-resolves verbatim against its immutable revision
  - id: Y03
    name: cross-references are edges
    assert: the 45 Parts carrying in-text cross-references resolve to REFERS_TO
      edges; reference closure is computed by traversal, not retrieval
  - id: Y04
    name: exception override
    assert: a CU judged unmet triggers a separate override call over its reference
      closure; a planted exception overturns the finding and is cited
  - id: Y05
    name: the organization graph exists
    assert: commitments, controls, roles, systems, activities and evidence specs are
      extracted from document text with resolving anchors; no row is a path-derived
      template or a constant string
  - id: Y06
    name: symmetric extraction discipline
    assert: internal fidelity round-trip is 100% on written commitments and internal
      completeness derives its denominator from document-declared structure
  - id: Y07
    name: vocabulary bridge
    assert: actor alignment resolves through recorded hypernym proposals marked
      STRONG when premise-supported; assessment.py contains no organization name or
      role-word literal
  - id: Y08
    name: the gate runs before the council
    assert: no model call receives un-pre-analyzed input; applicability, actor
      alignment, reference closure and constraint arithmetic are computed first
  - id: Y09
    name: listwise judgment
    assert: the council judges a CU plan in one call per anchor, not one call per
      atom; the packet is structured JSON; inference from silence is forbidden in
      the contract and tested
  - id: Y10
    name: four finding types
    assert: GAP, CONTRADICTION, OUTDATED_LANGUAGE and WEAK_MAPPING are each produced
      by their own detector; OUTDATED_LANGUAGE is deterministic against version and
      glossary lineage
  - id: Y11
    name: change taxonomy
    assert: every diff row carries a type from the taxonomy; DEFINITION_CHANGE with
      unchanged Part text still invalidates dependent determinations; RENUMBER_ONLY
      and EDITORIAL_ONLY create no review work
  - id: Y12
    name: Q05 is a bitemporal join
    assert: the baseline date comes from the internal document's own control block
      and is quoted; review-overdue is distinguished from substan
